# Gemini Fn-layer keys for the X desktop (started by
# /etc/xdg/autostart/gemini-keys.desktop). The Fn key is XKB level 3
# (Mod5, mask 0x80); keys are bound by raw keycode because shortcut daemons
# look up the XF86 keysyms on their standard keycodes and never match the
# Gemini's Fn layer (same issue GNOME had on NixOS). xkb keycode = evdev + 8:
#   Fn+B = 0x38 (56)  brightness down     Fn+N = 0x39 (57)  brightness up
# Override per user with ~/.xbindkeysrc (then edit the autostart Exec).
"brightnessctl --min-value=10 set 10%-"
    m:0x80 + c:56
"brightnessctl set 10%+"
    m:0x80 + c:57
